1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:05,304
On Saturday morning, Aziz opens the mobile bank to send money to his mother.

2
00:00:05,354 --> 00:00:07,632
He types the amount and taps Send.

3
00:00:07,682 --> 00:00:10,752
The money does not move, and no error appears.

4
00:00:10,802 --> 00:00:14,136
Instead, a screen full of text opens.

5
00:00:14,186 --> 00:00:18,996
So why does the bank show him text, and not the transfer?

6
00:00:19,046 --> 00:00:21,180
Aziz became a customer last Sunday.

7
00:00:21,230 --> 00:00:27,612
He has a number that TAF checked, a code that came to this phone, and a password that nobody can read.

8
00:00:27,662 --> 00:00:32,220
All of that is level one: the bank knows his phone, but not yet the person.

9
00:00:32,270 --> 00:00:36,708
Today he starts the way to level two, and this screen is the first step.

10
00:00:36,758 --> 00:00:42,540
Each app of the bank has a line in the installation: a name, a kind and a required level.

11
00:00:42,590 --> 00:00:46,356
The required level is the lowest level that the app asks for.

12
00:00:46,406 --> 00:00:51,300
The mobile bank has required level one, so Aziz used it right after registration.

13
00:00:51,350 --> 00:00:54,324
The app's own data needs only level one.

14
00:00:54,374 --> 00:01:01,836
But money needs level two, and so does data from the verified identity, like the verified address, cards or accounts.

15
00:01:01,886 --> 00:01:05,796
A transfer is money, so the transfer asks for level two.

16
00:01:05,846 --> 00:01:08,916
The easy answer is a red error: not allowed.

17
00:01:08,966 --> 00:01:11,004
The platform never gives that answer.

18
00:01:11,054 --> 00:01:17,652
Instead, the app asks for a step-up: the way from the level that Aziz has to the level that the action needs.

19
00:01:17,702 --> 00:01:19,524
The answer has three parts.

20
00:01:19,574 --> 00:01:21,396
The current level: one.

21
00:01:21,446 --> 00:01:23,292
The required level: two.

22
00:01:23,342 --> 00:01:30,084
And the checks that give level two: consent, a MyID check and a phone check, all in the mobile bank.

23
00:01:30,134 --> 00:01:32,796
Only the MyID check gives level two.

24
00:01:32,846 --> 00:01:36,036
No app, no operator and no setting can give it.

25
00:01:36,086 --> 00:01:39,708
So the app does not say no; it shows Aziz the way up.

26
00:01:39,758 --> 00:01:43,668
The first check is this screen of text: the consent gate.

27
00:01:43,718 --> 00:01:48,804
It stands before every call to MyID, and nothing reaches MyID around it.

28
00:01:48,854 --> 00:01:50,820
The screen has four fixed parts.

29
00:01:50,870 --> 00:02:03,876
The first part is the data that MyID reads from the state records: his names, his date and place of birth, his personal identification number, gender, citizenship, nationality, document data, registered addresses and phone number.

30
00:02:03,926 --> 00:02:06,756
The second part is the provider: MyID.

31
00:02:06,806 --> 00:02:11,364
The third part is the purpose: to identify him as a customer of this bank.

32
00:02:11,414 --> 00:02:16,284
The fourth part says who can read the data later: the bank's channels and its operators.

33
00:02:16,334 --> 00:02:23,412
It also says that TAF gets one thing, his personal identification number, for two checks after MyID.

34
00:02:23,462 --> 00:02:27,516
The bank writes the words of each part, but it cannot remove a part.

35
00:02:27,566 --> 00:02:28,980
The words come in versions.

36
00:02:29,030 --> 00:02:38,436
Each consent text and each terms text exists in the four languages of the installation: Uzbek Latin, Uzbek Cyrillic, Russian and English.

37
00:02:38,486 --> 00:02:44,820
Each version has a publication date, the staff user who proposed it, and a second staff user who approved it.

38
00:02:44,870 --> 00:02:50,844
The product ships a default text, compliance can change it, and the platform keeps every version.

39
00:02:50,894 --> 00:02:56,364
The screen always shows the version that is published at that moment, in the language of Aziz's journey.

40
00:02:56,414 --> 00:03:00,108
Aziz reads the fourth part twice, and taps Refuse.

41
00:03:00,158 --> 00:03:02,748
The platform opens no session at MyID.

42
00:03:02,798 --> 00:03:05,988
It counts no attempt, and Aziz stays at level one.

43
00:03:06,038 --> 00:03:09,228
It writes down only one thing: he refused.

44
00:03:09,278 --> 00:03:13,404
The money for his mother waits, but saying no costs Aziz nothing.

45
00:03:13,454 --> 00:03:15,108
That keeps the choice honest.

46
00:03:15,158 --> 00:03:19,668
In the afternoon, his mother calls: the rent is due on Monday.

47
00:03:19,718 --> 00:03:22,980
Aziz taps Send again, and the screen comes back.

48
00:03:23,030 --> 00:03:25,332
Nothing on it is selected in advance.

49
00:03:25,382 --> 00:03:29,748
His first answer is not copied, and no earlier yes ever counts.

50
00:03:29,798 --> 00:03:32,676
This time he reads to the end and taps Accept.

51
00:03:32,726 --> 00:03:36,708
Before any other step, the platform writes a record of his answer.

52
00:03:36,758 --> 00:03:45,012
It holds the versions of the consent text and the terms text, the language, the date and time, the device, the purpose, and Aziz.

53
00:03:45,062 --> 00:03:48,252
Only then may the platform open a session at MyID.

54
00:03:48,302 --> 00:03:51,036
One yes opens one session, no more.

55
00:03:51,086 --> 00:03:56,340
The record names the session that it allowed, so nobody can use the same yes twice.

56
00:03:56,390 --> 00:03:58,212
There is one more case.

57
00:03:58,262 --> 00:04:01,884
Suppose Aziz opens the screen and reads slowly.

58
00:04:01,934 --> 00:04:06,228
Meanwhile, compliance publishes a new version with a changed purpose.

59
00:04:06,278 --> 00:04:08,748
Aziz taps Accept on the old text.

60
00:04:08,798 --> 00:04:12,324
The platform refuses that answer and shows him the new text.

61
00:04:12,374 --> 00:04:16,500
The record must name exactly the version that he saw, word for word.

62
00:04:16,550 --> 00:04:22,860
On the map, the consent gate lives in the customer gateway, and the records of each answer live in Postgres.

63
00:04:22,910 --> 00:04:26,340
The mobile bank only shows the screen and sends the answer.

64
00:04:26,390 --> 00:04:28,212
Now a check for you.

65
00:04:28,262 --> 00:04:35,440
Aziz taps Refuse: how many MyID attempts does the platform count?

66
00:04:35,490 --> 00:04:38,848
None, because a refusal opens nothing at MyID.

67
00:04:38,898 --> 00:04:42,328
Each app has a required level, and money needs level two.

68
00:04:42,378 --> 00:04:48,808
When the level is too low, the platform does not refuse: the step-up names the level and the checks.

69
00:04:48,858 --> 00:04:53,416
The consent gate comes first, with four fixed parts and the published version.

70
00:04:53,466 --> 00:04:57,088
One yes opens one session, and a no costs nothing.

71
00:04:57,138 --> 00:05:01,312
Aziz has said yes, and the transfer to his mother waits for MyID.

72
00:05:01,362 --> 00:05:05,200
Lesson 13 opens the MyID check itself.
